TI  - From physical being to ecological becoming - Pilot studies of sustainable community development in China
T2  - RESEARCH IN HUMAN ECOLOGY: AN INTERDISCIPLINARY OVERVIEW
CP  - Symposium on the Occasion of the VII International Congress of Ecology (INTECOL)
AB  - Rooted in ancient Chinese human ecological philosophy, sustainable development in China is focused on design and remaking of the technological process, the institutional structure, and the harmonious function of the human ecosystem. This should be realised through cultivation of the totally functioning technology, systematically responsible institution and ecologically vivid culture. Pilot projects have been initiated using both a top down and a bottom up approach. They include more than 50 provincial and 29 national Comprehensive Experimental Communities for Sustainable Development, 51 national eco-counties and 100 ecological demonstration districts. Introduced here are five examples of these pilot studies: Baiquan hilly region eco-agriculture and ecosystem restoration with significant social-economic benefits; Xishan's eco-village development with landscape planning and comprehensive ecological engineering; Jinghua's eco-toilets and eco-building development combining the facets of greening, energy saving, waste recycling and land reclamation; Guanghan's household garbage recycling aiming at waste reduction. disinfection, regeneration, industrialisation and systematisation; Dafeng's eco-county promoting ecological agriculture, ecological industry, ecosystem conservation and community development.
