TI  - REMOVAL OF EFFECTS OF UNEVEN GRAZING IN PASTURE EXPERIMENTS
T2  - JOURNAL OF THE BRITISH GRASSLAND SOCIETY
AB  - An experiment is described in which uneven grazing by sheep introduced as bias in a white clover variety trial. The data were adjusted by covariance, using as the independent variable the position of the plots within the paddocks. Attention is drawn to the errors that may result from uneven grazing and a comparison is made with errors due to transference of fertility. Means of avoiding similar occurrences are suggested.
